/*
:name: loop_carry_kinds_3
:set: compile.cprop.engine=aegraph
:lec_expect: proven
*/
// HEADER-ONLY variant: the source is loop_carry_kinds.prp, compiled by the
// acyclic e-graph engine (pass.aegraph) instead of classic cprop. The base side
// stays on the default engine, so this pair proves "aegraph == classic" for the
// three loop carry shapes at once.
//
// The loops stay ROLLED (compile.unroll defaults false), so the aegraph meets
// compact-loop Subs (Subnode_loop): each Sub is a skeleton leaf whose carry
// self-edge must survive forwarding, and the loop body definition is optimized
// as its own graph. With no rewrite rules the engine only shares and folds, so
// the claim is that hash-consing, constant folding and the loop-carry guard
// preserve every carry.
